@page "/about"
<PageTitle>About · Budget Summary</PageTitle>
<h1 class="page-title">About</h1>

<div class="card">
    <p><strong>Budget Summary</strong> is a cross-platform budget analyzer built on
    <strong>Blazor WebAssembly</strong> with a <strong>functional core</strong>.</p>

    <h3 style="margin-top:1rem;">Architecture</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><code>Result&lt;T, DomainError&gt;</code> — railway-oriented error handling; no exceptions in the domain.</li>
        <li><code>Maybe&lt;T&gt;</code> — explicit optional values (sealed <code>Some</code>/<code>None</code>).</li>
        <li><code>BudgetWorkflow</code> — pure state machine: <code>Draft → Validated → Taxed → Receipt</code>.</li>
        <li><code>BudgetWorkflowRunner.EnrichExpenses</code> — composes validation + native tax + curried scoring.</li>
        <li><code>Scoring.CreateScore()</code> — curried, so you can swap score configs on the same data.</li>
        <li>Native tax via P/Invoke on desktop; <strong>pure managed fallback</strong> in the browser.</li>
    </ul>

    <p style="margin-top:1rem;">The same core assembly is exercised by <strong>24 xUnit tests</strong>
    via <code>dotnet test</code> in the console project.</p>
</div>